From 099649656458ca86803e1c5d544851ad23c753ce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: caoanhhao <caoanhhao@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 12:07:51 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] vtest: add VCMD_ALLOC_DMABUF_IMAGE (protocol version 6)

Let a vtest client (e.g. an Android gralloc) allocate window buffers on
the host GPU and get them back as dma-bufs with the host's real DRM
format modifier, so the buffers can be rendered by Venus and scanned
out / composited by a host compositor without copies.

The request carries width, height, a single-plane DRM fourcc, usage
flags (render / texture / scanout) and an optional list of allowed
modifiers (e.g. the compositor's).  The server intersects that list
with the device's exportable modifiers that have the needed tiling
features, creates a VkImage with VkImageDrmFormatModifierListCreateInfoEXT
and dedicated, exportable device-local memory, and replies with the
chosen modifier, row pitch, offset and size, followed by the dma-buf
fd over SCM_RIGHTS.  Errors are returned as a positive errno and keep
the connection.

The allocator lives in the vtest server process (vtest_vk_alloc.c,
libvulkan is dlopen'ed) with its own VkDevice on the --rendernode GPU,
matched through VK_EXT_physical_device_drm.  It is stateless: the
image and memory are released right after export and the dma-buf keeps
the allocation alive.  The command does not need a venus context.

